### Next.js-Security

- Treat every Server Action as a public endpoint: validate its input and verify authentication and authorization inside it; it is reachable by direct POST, whatever the page or the request boundary checked.
- Never read a secret through a `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable: Next.js includes those variables in the client bundle; read a server-only variable in a module marked with `import "server-only"`.
